<section class="sub-hero"><div class="sub-hero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/layton.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/layton-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/layton.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"></div><div class="shell sub-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">›</span><a href="/utah-communities/">Communities</a><span class="sep">›</span><span aria-current="page">Layton</span></nav><p class="kicker">Northern Wasatch · Davis County</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Layton, Utah</h1><p class="lede">Davis County’s largest city sits in the path of the powerful east winds that have twice in recent memory torn through the county, damaging roofs, fences and thousands of trees.</p><div class="row-btns"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-l" href="/contact-utah-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Davis County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Northern Wasatch</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="shell two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="callout"><b>Local claim risks</b><ul class="chips"><li>Canyon wind</li><li>Fallen trees</li><li>Hail</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Water losses</li></ul></div>
<h2>In the windstorm corridor</h2>
<p>Layton, along with Kaysville, Fruit Heights, Farmington and Centerville, lies beneath the steep western face of the Wasatch. On December 1, 2011, and again on September 8, 2020, downslope winds with hurricane-force gusts swept through Davis County, toppling trees, peeling roofs and damaging fences and outbuildings across thousands of properties.</p>
<h2>Typical claims</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Wind:</strong> roof, siding, gutter and fence damage, often across entire neighborhoods.</li>
<li><strong>Trees:</strong> mature trees falling onto homes, cars and outbuildings, with removal and debris costs.</li>
<li><strong>Hail and summer storms:</strong> roof and exterior damage.</li>
<li><strong>Winter:</strong> ice dams and frozen pipes, especially in East Layton homes nearer the mountains.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Housing notes</h2>
<p>Layton neighborhoods range from 1960s–70s homes near Hill Air Force Base and the original town center to newer subdivisions in East Layton. Many homes have vinyl or aluminum siding and wood fences that are hard to match after wind damage.</p>
<h2>What to check in your estimate</h2>
<p>Full-elevation siding replacement where pieces can’t be matched, complete fence runs and tree removal and debris costs are the most frequent gaps in Layton wind claims.</p>
<h2>Services for Layton property owners</h2><p>Every Utah Insurance Appraiser service is available in Layton and across Davis County, including:</p><ul class="cols2"><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/policy-appraisal-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/hail-roof-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/canyon-wind-damage-appraisal/">Wind &amp; Tornado Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/snow-ice-freeze-appraisal/">Snow Load, Ice Dam &amp; Freeze Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/water-pipe-leak-appraisal/">Water &amp; Leak Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul><h2>Questions from Layton owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>My neighbor got a new roof after the windstorm but I didn’t. Why?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Every claim is evaluated on its own damage and policy. Documentation matters. An estimate review can show whether your claim was scoped fully.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are fences covered after a windstorm?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Many policies cover fences as other structures, subject to limits and deductibles.</p></div></details></div><h2>Nearby communities</h2><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel" href="/utah-communities/ogden/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Ogden</span><svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/